title:: reAmbi
summary:: Ambisonic output chains and stereo monitors as objects
categories:: Libraries>reAmbi
related:: Classes/RAOutputChain, Classes/RAStereoMonitor, Guides/reCurrent

section:: What it is

The pieces of HomewareSC monitored their ambisonic mix through three NodeProxies (signal, transformer, decoder) created in a routine and chained by hand, with reverbs and all-pass stages moved into place with waits and code::moveAfter::. reAmbi makes that one object, link::Classes/RAOutputChain::, held by the song (link::Classes/RCSong#-addOutput::, code::~song.ambi::), plus link::Classes/RAStereoMonitor:: for the PA feed.

list::
## The chain is configured at boot and built at scene/init, after the song's node tree exists: its channel count, order and buses are valid before build.
## build is synchronous: groups created in order, proxies placed, links set before sources, the decoder played into its own group. No waits, no moves.
## Stages are inserted, removed and moved live with the other stages untouched.
## clear frees the groups first, then the proxies: the song can free its output group right after, with no late message.
## With the server stopped everything works client-side (tests, NRT), sending nothing.
::

section:: Usage

code::
(
// at boot (Common/Rc_Session)
~song.addOutput(\main, RAOutputChain(s, hoa_order_output, \main,
	decode: if(binaural) { \binaural } { \ambix },
	outBus: if(binaural) { cue_output_bus } { ambix_output_bus }));
)
// at scene/init, after makeGroups
~song.buildOutputs;

// instrument files
~song.ambi.signal.source = { ... };                       // the mix
~song.ambi.transformer.source = { LPF.ar(\in.ar(0 ! 16), 4000) };
~reverb = ~song.ambi.insert(\reverb, { ... \in.ar(0 ! 16) ... });   // before the decoder
~song.ambi.move(\reverb, after: \signal);
~song.ambi.addMonitor(RAStereoMonitor(16, 18, 5.0, 131/2, 0.5));
~song.ambi.bus(\decoder);                                 // for a recorder
::

section:: Decoder settings

Set at boot or later, taken at the next build (a change on a built chain posts "takes effect at the next build"):

list::
## code::hpFreq:: (20): a 4th-order high-pass on every channel before the decoder, nil for none. It keeps DC and sub-audio off the speakers.
## code::nearFieldExport:: (true): the decoders move the field from ATK's reference radius (1.5 m, where a basic encoding sits) to code::refRadius:: (AmbiX, 10 m: ATK's Format-Exchange recipe for "about infinity") or code::binauralRadius:: (3.25 m) with link::Classes/HoaNFCtrl::. That is the proximity bass of a 1.5 m source heard from the array: orders 1/2/3 +1.3/+5.1/+12.9 dB at 60 Hz, +3.8/+13.5/+28.2 dB at 30 Hz, unity above 500 Hz. Headphones hide it (the ear signals' bass is W's), a loudspeaker array plays it. code::false:: leaves the control filter out: the field leaves as plane waves, what an AmbiX decoder assumes, and a source's own near field (code::HoaNFCtrl.ar(sig, dist, AtkHoa.refRadius):: in the instrument) is flat at 1.5 m, lifted nearer, thinned farther. The stereo monitor's first-order link::Classes/FoaProximity:: follows it. An A/B in the room: code::~song.ambi.nearFieldExport = true:: (or false), then the scene init rebuilds the chain.
::

section:: Binaural decoding

The binaural decoder needs the HRTF buffers of its order. link::Classes/RAOutputChain#*loadBinauralIRs:: loads them per order with a completion callback; a chain built before they are in gets its decoder synth when they arrive (the proxy, its group and links exist at once). A server reboot forgets the cache.
